@{ Layout = "_LayoutPublic"; ViewData["Title"] = "Pilot to Production"; }
<section class="spx-page-hero"><div class="container">
  <span class="spx-kicker">Honest deployment path</span>
  <h1>Pilot to production: what a real deployment actually requires</h1>
  <p>Smart Port is a working enterprise AI operations prototype running on <strong>synthetic demo data</strong>. The engine, workflows, audit trail and approval gates are real and run today. What separates this prototype from a live port deployment is integration, data-sharing agreements and a security review — set out honestly below. No live port, customer, government or partnership relationship is claimed.</p>
</div></section>

<section class="spx-section spx-section--deep"><div class="container">
  <div class="spx-section__head">
    <span class="spx-kicker">Where we are today</span>
    <h2>Prototype stage — real engine, synthetic signals</h2>
    <p>Everything you can click in the demo is functional. The difference is the source of the data and the legal/technical agreements required to wire it to a live terminal.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="spx-card-grid spx-card-grid--three">
    <article class="spx-product"><span></span><h3>✅ Working today</h3><p>Cross-domain reasoning engine, deterministic fallback, execution-plan workflow, human approval gates, immutable audit trail, driver companion, fleet tracker rendered from check-ins, emissions/idling impact maths and role-based access control.</p></article>
    <article class="spx-product"><span></span><h3>🧪 Synthetic, by design</h3><p>Telematics, GPS, gate, berth, yard, container, disruption and emissions feeds are generated by demo connectors. The data shape mirrors real port feeds so connectors can be swapped without rewriting the engine.</p></article>
    <article class="spx-product"><span></span><h3>🔌 Connector-ready, not connected</h3><p>Integration adapters expose the interfaces a production feed would implement (TOS/IPMS, SCADA, telematics, AMI, mobile API). None are wired to a live system in this submission.</p></article>
  </div>
</div></section>

<section class="spx-section"><div class="container">
  <div class="spx-section__head">
    <span class="spx-kicker">The deployment checklist</span>
    <h2>What production requires</h2>
    <p>A real rollout is a joint programme with the port and fleet operators. These are the concrete gates between this prototype and a production system.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="spx-loop">
    <div class="spx-loop-step"><span>1</span><h3>Data-sharing agreements</h3><p>Signed agreements with the port authority and each fleet operator covering what operational data is shared, retention, and driver location consent. Nothing flows without them.</p></div>
    <div class="spx-loop-step"><span>2</span><h3>System integration</h3><p>Replace demo connectors with live adapters: Terminal Operating System (TOS/IPMS), gate/weighbridge SCADA, fleet telematics/GPS, ERP appointment booking, and a hardened mobile API for drivers.</p></div>
    <div class="spx-loop-step"><span>3</span><h3>Security &amp; compliance review</h3><p>Independent security review, penetration test, SSO/identity federation, data-residency confirmation, audit-log retention policy and a privacy assessment for driver location data.</p></div>
    <div class="spx-loop-step"><span>4</span><h3>Operational acceptance</h3><p>A controlled pilot with approved test drivers, baseline-vs-current metrics, an agreed SLA, an incident runbook and an operator training plan before any wider rollout.</p></div>
  </div>
</div></section>

<section class="spx-section spx-section--deep"><div class="container">
  <div class="spx-section__head">
    <span class="spx-kicker">Integration surface</span>
    <h2>Connectors a production deployment would wire up</h2>
  </div>
  <div class="spx-feature-matrix">
    <article><h3>Terminal Operating System</h3><p>Berth schedules, yard occupancy, container dwell and appointment windows from TOS/IPMS — today served by the demo port-ops provider.</p></article>
    <article><h3>Gate &amp; weighbridge (SCADA)</h3><p>Live gate throughput, lane status and weighbridge events to drive real backlog metering instead of synthetic gate capacity.</p></article>
    <article><h3>Fleet telematics / GPS</h3><p>Vehicle position and engine/idling data from fleet telematics, complementing — not replacing — explicit driver check-ins.</p></article>
    <article><h3>Mobile driver API</h3><p>Hardened, authenticated API for the driver companion: assigned job, queue position, instructions and tap-to-check-in.</p></article>
    <article><h3>Energy / AMI</h3><p>Advanced metering and load-shedding signals to anticipate energy-driven disruption to reefer and crane operations.</p></article>
    <article><h3>Messaging connector</h3><p>Optional WhatsApp Cloud API or push for driver notifications — consent-gated, framed as connector-ready in the demo.</p></article>
  </div>
</div></section>

